@server = http://localhost:4001
@me = alice
@other = bob
@conversation = dm:alice:bob

### Health: 200 when Cassandra, Redis and Kafka all answer; 503 lists what is down
GET {{server}}/health

### Register (or "log in" as) a username - there is no password
POST {{server}}/users
content-type: application/json

{ "username": "{{me}}" }

### Register the other side too
POST {{server}}/users
content-type: application/json

{ "username": "{{other}}" }

### Does a user exist?
GET {{server}}/users/{{other}}

### Start (or reopen) a 1:1 chat; the id is dm:<a>:<b>, sorted
POST {{server}}/conversations/direct
x-username: {{me}}
content-type: application/json

{ "with": "{{other}}" }

### My conversations, most recent first
GET {{server}}/conversations
x-username: {{me}}

### Conversation detail with members
GET {{server}}/conversations/{{conversation}}
x-username: {{me}}

### Send: 202 once Kafka has it. Re-send with the same clientMsgId: same messageId, stored once
POST {{server}}/conversations/{{conversation}}/messages
x-username: {{me}}
content-type: application/json

{ "clientMsgId": "6f1c2d3e-0000-4000-8000-000000000001", "body": "hello" }

### Newest page (oldest first in the response); hasMore = older pages exist
GET {{server}}/conversations/{{conversation}}/messages?limit=20
x-username: {{me}}

### Older page: before = the oldest messageId you have
GET {{server}}/conversations/{{conversation}}/messages?limit=20&before=<messageId>
x-username: {{me}}

### Catch up: after = the newest messageId you have
GET {{server}}/conversations/{{conversation}}/messages?after=<messageId>
x-username: {{me}}

### WebSocket (not an HTTP request): ws://localhost:4001/ws
# 1. send {"type":"hello","username":"alice"}            -> {"type":"ready",...}
# 2. send {"type":"send","conversationId":"dm:alice:bob","clientMsgId":"<uuid>","body":"hi"}
#                                                          -> {"type":"ack",...} then {"type":"message",...}

### Through nginx (both servers): the "server" field alternates
GET http://localhost:4000/health

### Presence: online, or offline with lastSeen
GET {{server}}/users/{{other}}/presence

# WebSocket: {"type":"watch","usernames":["bob"]} -> {"type":"presence","username":"bob","online":true,...}

# WebSocket: {"type":"receipt","conversationId":"dm:alice:bob","status":"read","upTo":"<messageId>"}
#   -> every member gets {"type":"receipt",...}; GET /conversations/:id shows each member's watermarks
# WebSocket: {"type":"typing","conversationId":"dm:alice:bob"} -> the others get {"type":"typing",...}
